div.p:
The President and his cabinet hold the dispatch of public affairs in the most
                    complete disregard, without attending to it further than their personal
                    pleasures dictate to the scandal of honest men and to the scoff of society;

The municipal power has disappeared completely, and the ayuntamientos, (city
                    councils,) officers of a superior order, have been converted into humble
                    dependents upon the governors and prefects;

Whereas the abuse, already elevated to a regular system, of each one of the protégés of the President or of his friends, having
                    three and even four positions, and receiving three and four salaries, corrupts
                    good administrations;
